","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":3,"target_pdf_page":540,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":{"pdf":540,"by":"section","key":"1030","file":"usc18@119-111.pdf"},"target_columns":[]},{"src_doc":"DDC-077","src_page":"4","text":"ECF 74 at 48","n":"1","kind":"ecf","target_doc":"DDC-074","target_page":"48","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"at 48","status":"verified","target_quote":"does not rest the Wiretap Act's contents element on Comcast","line":38,"k":1,"unit_id":"DDC-077-4-1-1-5b6cc99f","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":4,"target_pdf_page":48,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null,"target_columns":[]},{"src_doc":"DDC-077","src_page":"4","text":"18 U.S.C. § 2511","n":"1","kind":"statute","target_doc":"usc-18-chapter-119-wire-and-electronic-communications-interception-and-interception-of-oral-communications","target_page":"1070","target_page_end":"1071","target_pin":"§ 2511","status":"verified","target_quote":"(1) Except as otherwise specifically provided in this chapter any person who-(a) intentionally intercepts, endeavors to intercept, or procures any other person to intercept or [Release Point 119-111] endeavor to intercept, any wire, oral, or electronic communication;","line":39,"k":1,"unit_id":"DDC-077-4-1-1-2a311a78","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":4,"target_pdf_page":1070,"target_pdf_page_end":1071,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null,"target_columns":[]},{"src_doc":"DDC-077","src_page":"4","text":"§ 1030","n":"1","kind":"statute","target_doc":"usc-18-chapter-047-fraud-and-false-statements","target_page":"540","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"§ 1030","status":"mapped","target_quote":"(2) intentionally accesses a computer without authorization or exceeds authorized access, and thereby obtains-... (C) information from any protected computer;","line":40,"k":1,"unit_id":"DDC-077-4-1-1-8e842d1e","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":4,"target_pdf_page":540,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null,"target_columns":[]},{"src_doc":"DDC-077","src_page":"4","text":"ECF 57 at 16–17","n":"1","kind":"ecf","target_doc":"DDC-057","target_page":"16","target_page_end":"17","target_pin":"at 16–17","status":"verified","target_quote":"","line":41,"k":1,"unit_id":"DDC-077-4-1-1-fdfafa3f","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":4,"target_pdf_page":16,"target_pdf_page_end":17,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null,"target_columns":null},{"src_doc":"DDC-077","src_page":"4","text":"ECF 51-54 at 116","n":"1","kind":"ecf","target_doc":"DDC-051-54","target_page":"116","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"at 116","status":"verified","target_quote":"","line":42,"k":1,"unit_id":"DDC-077-4-1-1-dfa67c4f","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":4,"target_pdf_page":116,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null,"target_columns":null},{"src_doc":"DDC-077","src_page":"4","text":"Alice Corp. Pty. Ltd. v. CLS Bank Int'l, 573 U.S. 208, 225 (2014)","n":"1","kind":"case","target_doc":"2014 - Alice Corp. v. CLS Bank International, 573 U.S. 208","target_page":"225","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"573 U.S. at 225","status":"verified","target_quote":"In light of the foregoing, see supra, at 222, the relevant question is whether the claims here do more than simply instruct the practitioner to implement the abstract idea of intermediated settlement on a generic computer. They do not … In short, each step does no more than require a generic computer to perform generic computer functions. Considered \"as an ordered combination,\" the computer components of petitioner's method \"ad[d] nothing . . . that is not already present when the steps are considered separately. \" Id., at 79. Viewed as a whole, petitioner 's method claims simply recite the concept of intermediated settlement as performed by a generic computer","line":43,"k":1,"unit_id":"DDC-077-4-1-1-f77dc35a","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":4,"target_pdf_page":18,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null,"target_columns":[]},{"src_doc":"DDC-077","src_page":"4","text":"Thaler v. Perlmutter, 130 F.4th 1039, 1046, 1048 (D.C. Cir. 2025)","n":"1","kind":"case","target_doc":"2025 - Thaler v. Perlmutter, 130 F.4th 1039","target_page":"12","target_page_end":"17","target_pin":"130 F.4th at 1046, 1048 (slip 12, 17)","status":"verified","target_quote":"Machines lack minds and do not intend anything. Seventh, and by comparison, every time the Copyright Act discusses machines, the context indicates that machines are tools, not authors … Here, the Copyright Act makes no sense if an \"author\" is not a human being. If \"machine\" is substituted for \"author,\" the Copyright Act would refer to a machine's \"children,\" 17 U.S.C. § 203(a)(2), a machine's \"widow,\" id., a machine's \"domicile,\" id. § 104(a), a machine's mens rea, id. § 101, and a machine's \"nationality,\" id. Problematic questions would arise about a machine's \"life\" and \"death[.]\" Id. § 302(a). And \"machine\" would inconsistently mean both an author and a tool used by authors","line":44,"k":1,"unit_id":"DDC-077-4-1-1-011a72dc","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":4,"target_pdf_page":12,"target_pdf_page_end":17,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null,"target_columns":[]},{"src_doc":"DDC-077","src_page":"4","text":"ECF 75 at 27","n":"1","kind":"ecf","target_doc":"DDC-075","target_page":"27","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"at 27","status":"verified","target_quote":"an AI coding assistant","line":45,"k":1,"unit_id":"DDC-077-4-1-1-6b928a2b","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":4,"target_pdf_page":27,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null,"target_columns":[]},{"src_doc":"DDC-077","src_page":"4","text":"35 U.S.C. § 101","n":"1","kind":"statute","target_doc":"usc-35-chapter-010-patentability-of-inventions","target_page":"68","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"§ 101","status":"verified","target_quote":"Whoever invents or discovers any new and useful process, machine, manufacture, or composition of matter, or any new and useful improvement thereof, may obtain a patent therefor, subject to the conditions and requirements of this title.","line":46,"k":1,"unit_id":"DDC-077-4-1-1-065ca51f","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":4,"target_pdf_page":68,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null,"target_columns":[]},{"src_doc":"DDC-077","src_page":"4","text":"TAC ¶¶ 14, 67","n":"1","kind":"tac","target_doc":"DDC-051","target_page":"20","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"¶ 14","status":"verified","target_quote":"DANGEROUS_uncachedSystemPromptSection","line":47,"k":1,"unit_id":"DDC-077-4-1-1-701bb4d1","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":4,"target_pdf_page":20,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null,"target_columns":[]},{"src_doc":"DDC-077","src_page":"4","text":"TAC ¶¶ 14, 67","n":"1","kind":"tac","target_doc":"DDC-051","target_page":"49","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"¶ 67","status":"verified","target_quote":"DANGEROUS_uncachedSystemPromptSection","line":48,"k":2,"unit_id":"DDC-077-4-1-2-701bb4d1","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":4,"target_pdf_page":49,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null,"target_columns":[]},{"src_doc":"DDC-077","src_page":"4","text":"SC-4","n":"1","kind":"finding","target_doc":"DDC-051-55","target_page":"258","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"SC-4","status":"verified","target_quote":"","line":49,"k":1,"unit_id":"DDC-077-4-1-1-9b20f8c0","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":4,"target_pdf_page":258,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null,"target_columns":null},{"src_doc":"DDC-077","src_page":"4","text":"NF-37","n":"1","kind":"finding","target_doc":"DDC-051-55","target_page":"300","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"NF-37","status":"verified","target_q