ext":"ECF 70-1 at 43–45","n":"1","kind":"ecf","target_doc":"DDC-070-01","target_page":"54","target_page_end":"56","target_pin":"at 43–45","status":"verified","target_quote":"","line":72,"k":1,"unit_id":"DDC-077-5-1-1-ad503aaa","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":5,"target_pdf_page":54,"target_pdf_page_end":56,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null,"target_columns":null},{"src_doc":"DDC-077","src_page":"6","text":"Garcia v. Character Technologies, Inc., 2025 WL 1461721 (M.D. Fla. May 21, 2025)","n":"1","kind":"case","target_doc":"2025 - Garcia v. Character Technologies, Inc., No. 6:24-cv-01903-ACC-UAM (M.D. Fla. May 21, 2025), ECF 115","target_page":"","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"","status":"mapped","target_quote":"","line":73,"k":1,"unit_id":"DDC-077-6-1-1-293b8066","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":6,"target_pdf_page":null,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null,"target_columns":null},{"src_doc":"DDC-077","src_page":"6","text":"TAC ¶ 318","n":"1","kind":"tac","target_doc":"DDC-051","target_page":"214","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"¶ 318","status":"verified","target_quote":"within the meaning of strict product-liability doctrine under DC law and Minnesota law","line":74,"k":1,"unit_id":"DDC-077-6-1-1-6fd3cb03","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":6,"target_pdf_page":214,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null,"target_columns":[]},{"src_doc":"DDC-077","src_page":"6","text":"Betz v. Jefferson Cap. Sys., LLC, 68 F. Supp. 3d 130, 136 (D.D.C. 2014)","n":"1","kind":"case","target_doc":"2014 - Betz v. Jefferson Capital Systems, LLC, 68 F. Supp. 3d 130","target_page":"8","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"68 F. Supp. 3d at 136 (slip 8)","status":"verified","target_quote":"Plaintiff did not respond in his opposition to any of defendant's argument regarding his invasion of privacy claim. The Court accordingly treats those arguments as conceded, and will grant defendant's motion to dismiss plaintiff's invasion of privacy claim. See Ali v. D.C. Court Servs., 538 F. Supp. 2d 157, 161 (D.D.C. 2008) (\"If a plaintiff fails to respond to a motion to dismiss or files an opposition to a motion to dismiss addressing only certain arguments raised by the defendant, a court may treat those arguments that the plaintiff failed to address as conceded.\")","line":75,"k":1,"unit_id":"DDC-077-6-1-1-6061fd8e","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":6,"target_pdf_page":8,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null,"target_columns":[]},{"src_doc":"DDC-077","src_page":"6","text":"ECF 75 at 30","n":"1","kind":"ecf","target_doc":"DDC-075","target_page":"30","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"at 30","status":"verified","target_quote":"","line":76,"k":1,"unit_id":"DDC-077-6-1-1-3307c9c4","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":6,"target_pdf_page":30,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null,"target_columns":null},{"src_doc":"DDC-077","src_page":"6","text":"Hedgepeth v. Whitman Walker Clinic, 22 A.3d 789, 802 (D.C. 2011) (en banc)","n":"1","kind":"case","target_doc":"2011 - Hedgepeth v. Whitman Walker Clinic, 22 A.3d 789","target_page":"802","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"22 A.3d at 802","status":"verified","target_quote":"We agree with the draft Third Restatement and Professor Dobbs's observation that no special rule (such as the zone of physical danger test) is necessary to guard against the risk of imposing a duty that might be unlimited or unreasonable when emotional harm is especially likely to be caused as a direct result of negligent performance of a duty to avoid such harm owed to a specific person. Such a duty can, but need not, arise from a contractual arrangement between the … The key point is that the requirement of a special relationship between the parties or undertaking by the defendant to the plaintiff limits the scope of the defendant's potential liability to identifiable persons, rendering the \"zone of physical danger\" requirement unnecessary to achieve that purpose. Indeed, a number of courts around the country have held that a defendant has a duty to avoid causing emotional distress to a plaintiff if the defendant has undertaken an obligation to benefit the plaintiff and if that undertaking, by its nature, creates not only a foreseeable, but an especially likely, risk that the defendant's negligent performance of the obligation will cause serious emotional distress. This means that not every existing relationship or undertaking will suffice to create a duty to avoid the negligent infliction of emotional distress. Thus, courts consider the nature of the relationship between the parties and the likelihood that emotional distress will be caused by negligent performance of a recognized obligation before permitting stand-alone claims for emotional distress","line":77,"k":1,"unit_id":"DDC-077-6-1-1-171c9d53","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":6,"target_pdf_page":14,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null,"target_columns":[14]},{"src_doc":"DDC-077","src_page":"6","text":"ECF 74 at 57–58","n":"1","kind":"ecf","target_doc":"DDC-074","target_page":"57","target_page_end":"58","target_pin":"at 57–58","status":"verified","target_quote":"","line":78,"k":1,"unit_id":"DDC-077-6-1-1-ce359ecb","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":6,"target_pdf_page":57,"target_pdf_page_end":58,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null,"target_columns":null},{"src_doc":"DDC-077","src_page":"6","text":"ECF 74 at 57–58","n":"2","kind":"ecf","target_doc":"DDC-074","target_page":"57","target_page_end":"58","target_pin":"at 57–58","status":"verified","target_quote":"","line":79,"k":1,"unit_id":"DDC-077-6-2-1-ce359ecb","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":6,"target_pdf_page":57,"target_pdf_page_end":58,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null,"target_columns":null},{"src_doc":"DDC-077","src_page":"6","text":"ECF 75 at 29","n":"1","kind":"ecf","target_doc":"DDC-075","target_page":"29","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"at 29","status":"verified","target_quote":"clarifies that his claim against Anthropic and OpenAI rests on a special-relationship theory","line":80,"k":1,"unit_id":"DDC-077-6-1-1-4856a683","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":6,"target_pdf_page":29,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null,"target_columns":[]},{"src_doc":"DDC-077","src_page":"6","text":"Rule 8","n":"1","kind":"rule","target_doc":"Federal Rules of Civil Procedure (Dec. 1, 2025, uscourts.gov official pamphlet)","target_page":"15","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"Rule 8","status":"mapped","target_quote":"A pleading that states a claim for relief must contain: ... (2) a short and plain statement of the claim showing that the pleader is entitled to relief;","line":81,"k":1,"unit_id":"DDC-077-6-1-1-352e65d0","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":6,"target_pdf_page":34,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null,"target_columns":[]},{"src_doc":"DDC-077","src_page":"7","text":"ECF 75 at 31","n":"1","kind":"ecf","target_doc":"DDC-075","target_page":"31","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"at 31","status":"verified","target_quote":"discussing improper incorporation","line":82,"k":1,"unit_id":"DDC-077-7-1-1-f5b6add2","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":7,"target_pdf_page":31,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null,"target_columns":[]},{"src_doc":"DDC-077","src_page":"7","text":"ECF 75 at 8–9","n":"1","kind":"ecf","target_doc":"DDC-075","target_page":"8","target_page_end":"9","target_pin":"at 8–9","status":"verified","target_quote":"","line":83,"k":1,"unit_id":"DDC-077-7-1-1-4a9bc7ef","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":7,"target_pdf_page":8,"target_pdf_page_end":9,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null,"target_columns":null},{"src_doc":"DDC-077","src_page":"7","text":"Federal Rule of Civil Procedure 10(c)","n":"1","kind":"rule","target_doc":"Federal Rules of Civil Procedure (Dec. 1, 2025, uscourts.gov official pamphlet)","target_page":"18","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"Rule 10(c)","status":"mapped","target_quote":"A statement in a pleading may be adopted by reference elsewhere in the same pleading or in any other pleading or motion. A copy of a written instrument that is an exhibit to a pleading is a part of the pleading for all purposes.","line":84,"k":1,"unit_id":"DDC-077-7-1-1-e08fa60b","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":7,"target_pdf_page":37,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null,"target_columns":[]},{"src_doc":"DDC-077","src_page":"7","text":"ECF 74 at 7–10","n":"1","kind":"ecf","target_doc":"DDC-074","target_page":"7","target_page_end":"10","target_pin":"at 7–10","status":"verified","target_quote":"","line":85,"k":1,"unit_id":"DDC-077-7-1-1-388a4ed8","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":7,"target_pdf_page":7,"target_pdf_page_end":10,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null,"target_columns":null},{"src_doc":"DDC-077","src_page":"7","text":"ECF 75 at 21","n":"1","kind":"ecf","target_doc":"DDC-075","target_page":"21","target_page_end":"","target_pin":"at 21","status":"verified","target_quote":"neither Defendants nor the Court are obligated to hunt through thousands of pages of exhibits","line":86,"k":1,"unit_id":"DDC-077-7-1-1-18a7245a","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":7,"target_pdf_page":21,"target_pdf_page_end":null,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null,"target_columns":[]},{"src_doc":"DDC-077","src_page":"7","text":"ECF 74 at 9–10","n":"1","kind":"ecf","target_doc":"DDC-074","target_page":"9","target_page_end":"10","target_pin":"at 9–10","status":"verified","target_quote":"","line":87,"k":1,"unit_id":"DDC-077-7-1-1-fc5c864a","violations":[],"warnings":[],"src_pdf_page":7,"target_pdf_page":9,"target_pdf_page_end":10,"target_known":true,"target_pin_page":null,"target_column